{
 "_comment": [
  "News coverage of energy infrastructure siting in Oklahoma and the public",
  "response to it. The news half of ses_ok_yt, which does the same for",
  "YouTube comments; both read the same codebook, so their exports carry the",
  "same columns and can be stacked in a spreadsheet.",
  "",
  "Oklahoma only. Unlike YouTube, GDELT and Google News do respect a state",
  "name in a query, so state-level searching works here and there is no need",
  "to go county by county.",
  "",
  "Neither source needs a key, so nothing goes in repository secrets and",
  "there is no quota shared with the YouTube crawlers.",
  "",
  "Phrases with spaces must stay in quotes. subjects are what gets searched;",
  "recognize is the wider vocabulary used to judge whether a result belongs.",
  "Both engines reject long queries, so only the first six angles are used."
 ],
